==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etym|gmh|de}} {{term|roum|lang=gmh}}. The expected modern form would be ''Raum'', which has been ousted by a dialectal form due to the identicalness with {{term|Raum||room|lang=de}} (from Middle High German {{term|rūm|lang=gmh}}). Dialects that have developed Middle High German ''-ou-'' into ''-ā-'' are found in south-eastern and central-western Germany. Cognate with Dutch {{term|room|lang=nl}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʁaːm/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Rahm.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aːm|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m||gen2=Rahmes|-}}

# [[cream]] (milkfat)

====Usage notes====
In German standard German, ''Rahm'' is used mainly in compounds (such as ''Rahmsoße, Sauerrahm'' etc.); otherwise {{term|Sahne|lang=de}} is much more common. This is not necessarily true of colloquial varieties nor of standard German in Austria and Switzerland.

